-
-# Security tokens
-# Math.random is fine for non-security tokens (payment link slugs, OTP
-# codes). The uniqueness constraint on the DB column is what prevents
-# collisions, not the entropy source. Only session tokens and API keys
-# use crypto.randomBytes.
-
-# Float usage in Go
-# The float32 in batch.go is intentional — BD amounts only need 2 decimal
-# places of precision, and float32 gives 7 significant digits which is
-# more than enough for any realistic settlement batch. The int64 path is
